    "common_form_notes": "Widely stocked in sheet, plate, tube, and bar. 316L (low-carbon variant) preferred for welded assemblies to prevent sensitisation.",
    "usage_frequency": "Common",
    "notes": "Austenitic stainless steel with 2–3% Mo addition for superior chloride and pitting corrosion resistance compared to 304/303. Yield strength (200 MPa) is the EN 10088-3 minimum for annealed bar; ASTM A276 specifies a minimum of 207 MPa (30 ksi). Tensile strength 517 MPa is the ASTM A276 minimum of 75 ksi converted to metric. 316L (low carbon, ≤0.03% C) is preferred when welding and is the standard grade used for metal AM (DMLS/SLM and Binder Jet); the lower carbon content prevents sensitisation during the thermal cycles of AM and welding. Electrical conductivity derived from resistivity of 0.74 µΩ·m. Shear strength derived from von Mises criterion: UTS/√3 = 517/1.732 ≈ 299 MPa. Melting point is solidus; liquidus 1400°C (MatWeb)."
  },
  "typical_usage": "Marine hardware, boat fittings and fasteners; pharmaceutical and food-processing equipment; chemical process piping and vessels; surgical implants; architectural cladding in coastal environments; cryogenic components.",
